## Agent & Tool Selection Guide

Use the right tool for each phase of work. The wrong tool at the wrong time creates noise.

### Planning & exploration

| Task | Tool |
|------|------|
| Plan a non-trivial new feature | `/feature-dev` → selects code-architect or code-explorer automatically |
| Understand how an existing feature works | `feature-dev:code-explorer` |
| Clarify requirements with structured questions | `/jmo:interview` |
| Look up library API (React, Supabase, Capacitor, etc.) | Context7 MCP — triggered automatically by global rules |

### Implementation

| Task | Tool |
|------|------|
| Implement an already-planned feature | Claude directly (no sub-agent needed) |
| Apply a small targeted UI improvement | `/jmo:better-ui` |
| Improve visual design and aesthetic direction | `/frontend-design` |
| Refactor or simplify recently-changed code | `/simplify` |

### Review & validation

| Task | Tool |
|------|------|
| Check Sprig data safety (storage, dates, secrets) | `sprig-qa-reviewer` (project agent) |
| Check UI consistency (colors, haptics, animations) | `sprig-ui-reviewer` (project agent) |
| General code bugs and logic errors | `/code-review` |
| Security-specific review | `/security-review` |

### Testing & verification

| Task | Tool |
|------|------|
| Exploratory browser automation, screenshots | `/playwright-cli` (interactive, opens msedge) |
| Verify a specific change works in the browser | `/verify` |
| Run unit tests (after vitest installed) | `npm run test` |
| Run E2E tests (after @playwright/test installed) | `npx playwright test` |

### Database & deployment

| Task | Tool |
|------|------|
| Query or inspect Supabase schema/data | `/supabase` |
| Check Vercel deploy status, env vars, logs | Vercel MCP tools |
| Trigger Codemagic build → TestFlight | User must trigger manually at codemagic.io |

### ESLint note
`npx eslint src` has 15 pre-existing `react-hooks/purity` errors in `TodayTab.jsx`. These are known and do not block development. Do not use ESLint exit code as a quality gate; use Babel validation instead.

